# Cursor AI Rules — Arkhiveon (RPG Notes)

Always adhere to these guidelines when suggesting code, creating components, or refactoring in this repository.

## 1. Design System Check (Mandatory)
- Before creating or modifying UI components, inspect the Design System in `src/routes/design-system.tsx`.
- Use global semantic HSL tokens: `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `bg-card-elevated`, `text-primary`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border/70`.
- DO NOT hardcode solid arbitrary colors (e.g. `bg-[#1a1a1a]`, `text-[#ff0000]`).
- Include glassmorphism (`backdrop-blur-md`), smooth hover states (`transition-all duration-150 ease-out active:scale-[0.98]`), and responsive touch targets (min 44px on mobile).

## 2. Anti-useEffect Rule
- STRICTLY MINIMIZE / AVOID `useEffect`. Multiple `useEffect` hooks create exponential cognitive complexity, stale closures, race conditions, and infinite re-render loops.
- Use derived state during render or `useMemo`.
- Handle side effects directly inside user event handlers (`onClick`, `onChange`, `onSubmit`).
- Use Zustand actions or TanStack Router loaders/subscribers for store synchronization.
- Use `useDeferredValue` for input filtering instead of custom effects.

## 3. Zustand Performance & Selectors
- Selectors must return primitive values or stable references (`useRPGStore(state => state.characters)`).
- NEVER create new objects/arrays inside selector functions (e.g. `useRPGStore(state => state.items.filter(...))`), as this triggers infinite React render loops.
- Wrap heavy list filtering in `useMemo`.

## 4. Mobile-First Responsiveness
- All sheets, modals, forms, and cards must work seamlessly on mobile viewports (`grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2`).
- Touch targets must be at least 44px in height/width.
- Prevent horizontal scrollbars (`overflow-x`).

## 5. TypeScript & Biome Standards
- Avoid `any` types; define explicit TypeScript interfaces (`Character`, `SheetModuleConfig`, `Faction`, `Item`, `Npc`, `Lore`).
- Always run Biome check before completing changes: `npx @biomejs/biome check --write <modified_files>`.
- Ensure `pnpm run build` (`tsc`) completes with zero errors.

## 6. Package Manager & Git Rules
- Package manager: EXCLUSIVELY use `pnpm`. Never run `npm` or `yarn`.
- Branch prefixes: `garbini/*` for Luiz Garbini (`garbasneto@gmail.com`) and `arroyo/*` for Gabriel Arroyo (`gabrielarroyoc18@gmail.com`).

## 7. Automated E2E Video / Screenshot Preview Testing
Whenever completing any frontend feature or UI component, execute:
```bash
pnpm preview:record
```
This generates `docs/previews/latest-preview.webm` and `latest-preview.png` via Playwright.
- Note: `docs/previews/` is ignored by `.gitignore` to prevent Git bloat.
- Drag & drop the recorded video directly into GitHub PR description box to embed.

## 8. Mandatory Pull Request Description Format
Whenever pushing changes, completing a task, or preparing a branch for review, the AI MUST ALWAYS automatically provide a formatted, copy-paste ready Pull Request description following `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`:

```markdown
## ✨ What was added

- Clearly describe what was added or implemented in this PR.
Be specific and concise with bullet points.

## 📷 Implementation preview

<!-- Add screenshots or a short video showing the implemented feature.
Make sure the preview reflects the final behavior. -->
```
